This project is an interactive Weather & AQI Dashboard developed using Microsoft Power BI to analyze weather conditions and air quality insights through dynamic visualizations and KPI tracking. The dashboard transforms raw environmental data into meaningful insights for better understanding and analysis.

Features
Real-time weather analysis
AQI (Air Quality Index) monitoring
Rain prediction tracking
Humidity and UV index analysis
Interactive charts and KPI cards
User-friendly dashboard interface

Tools & Technologies Used: Power BI

Skills Demonstrated
Data Cleaning & Transformation
Data Visualization
Dashboard Development
KPI Analysis
Environmental Data Analysis
Business Intelligence Reporting

Insights: 
Air Quality Insights
Delhi consistently shows the worst air quality, likely due to: High population , Heavy vehicle density 
Imphal performs best, indicating cleaner environment and lower pollution sources. 

Traffic vs Visibility  : Clear negative correlation Higher vehicle count → Lower visibility 
This supports that vehicular pollution is a major contributor to AQI deterioration. 

Population Impact 
States with higher population (like Delhi,Maharashtra) have: Higher AQI levels, Greater pollution concentration 
Lower population states show comparatively better air quality 
Indicates urbanization directly impacts air pollution levels 

Temperature Trends : Slight increase in temperature from 2024 to 2025 Could indicate: Seasonal variation, Early signs of warming trends 

Recommendation: 
Limit outdoor activities, 
Promote public transport, 
Use air purifiers indoors, 
Maintain green cover, 
Encourage sustainable practices, 
Heat alerts, 
hydration awareness, 
Focus policies on worst

